  "text": "[warm] Step all the way out — you can have this. Four steps — each one rebuilt the map you saw. [short pause] One. Build the plan with an agent; argue until it survives you. The map rebuild's plan was forty-four dependent tasks. [short pause] Two. The agent scaffolds a ledger — the single source of truth — and a workflow that reads it. Then it stops. Nothing runs until you've read what it intends. [short pause] Three. Run it. Here is what that looks like — the map rebuild's ledger.\n\n\n\nA task is a block: type, status, dependencies, acceptance.\n\n\n\nA round is a verdict: the orchestrator re-ran the tests — thirty-seven of thirty-seven — before marking done.\n\n\n\nA death is a line item: an interrupted run left two files failing; the next run read the ledger and finished them. [short pause] Four. Watch from outside: sow a bug, throttle, pause. The overcrowded manor was healed that way. [pause] This is not a demo: the same skill has run real production work — a repository lift-and-shift, and the developer-experience passes that followed. Same ledger, same orchestrator, same stops. [short pause] Two lines are wall-mounted in the skill. One guards the return: metadata and pointers, never a payload. The other guards the stop: don't lower this bar, or the loop turns into a chat. [pause] The kit is yours. One layer remains.",
